Relevant columns for the task
customer_transactions."customer_id": customer identifier – used to group all transactions that belong to one account.  
customer_transactions."txn_date": transaction date – will be converted to month‑year so we know which month a transaction belongs to.  
customer_transactions."txn_type": deposit/withdrawal – decide the sign (+/‑) of each amount when calculating balances.  
customer_transactions."txn_amount": the amount of money moved for the transaction – used in all balance arithmetic.  

Optional helper columns / tables
strftime('%Y‑%m', customer_transactions."txn_date"): extract “YYYY‑MM” string for monthly grouping.  
(CROSS JOIN of distinct months found in the data) – gives a complete calendar so that customers with no activity in a month will still show a row with 0 change.  

Typical conditions that might be used
txn_type = 'deposit'            -- for positive cash‑flow  
txn_type = 'withdrawal'         -- for negative cash‑flow  
WHERE strftime('%Y', txn_date)=? -- pick a specific year, if required  
HAVING SUM(CASE …) <> 0         -- filter customers with non‑zero net change  
ORDER BY customer_id, month_year

Below are ten exploratory SQL statements (all capped at 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to building the final month‑end balance output.  

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: inspect distinct customer IDs present in the bank ledger
SELECT DISTINCT "customer_id"
FROM "customer_transactions"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: list the distinct transaction types recorded
SELECT DISTINCT "txn_type"
FROM "customer_transactions"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: fetch a handful of raw transactions for one customer (e.g. customer 1)
SELECT "customer_id",
       "txn_date",
       "txn_type",
       "txn_amount"
FROM   "customer_transactions"
WHERE  "customer_id" = 1
ORDER BY "txn_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: view all distinct calendar months that exist in the ledger
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year"
FROM   "customer_transactions"
ORDER  BY "month_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: calculate the signed amount (deposit = +, withdrawal = -) for each transaction
SELECT "customer_id",
       "txn_date",
       CASE 
            WHEN "txn_type" = 'deposit'    THEN  1 
            WHEN "txn_type" = 'withdrawal' THEN -1 
            ELSE 0 
       END * "txn_amount" AS "signed_amount"
FROM   "customer_transactions"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: total monthly net movement per customer (positive = net deposit, negative = net withdrawal)
SELECT "customer_id",
       strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year",
       SUM( CASE 
                WHEN "txn_type" = 'deposit'    THEN  "txn_amount"
                WHEN "txn_type" = 'withdrawal' THEN - "txn_amount"
                ELSE 0
           END ) AS "monthly_change"
FROM   "customer_transactions"
GROUP  BY "customer_id", "month_year"
ORDER  BY "customer_id", "month_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: derive the running (cumulative) balance for each customer, month by month
SELECT "customer_id",
       "month_year",
       "monthly_change",
       SUM("monthly_change") OVER (PARTITION BY "customer_id"
                                   ORDER BY "month_year") AS "cumulative_balance"
FROM (
      SELECT "customer_id",
             strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year",
             SUM( CASE 
                      WHEN "txn_type" = 'deposit'    THEN  "txn_amount"
                      WHEN "txn_type" = 'withdrawal' THEN - "txn_amount"
                      ELSE 0
                 END ) AS "monthly_change"
      FROM   "customer_transactions"
      GROUP  BY "customer_id", "month_year"
) AS m
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: generate a list of all customer‑month combinations (cartesian product) 
-- so that months with no activity still appear.
WITH all_months AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
), all_customers AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT "customer_id"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
)
SELECT c."customer_id",
       m."month_year"
FROM   all_customers  AS c
CROSS  JOIN all_months AS m
ORDER  BY c."customer_id", m."month_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣ Description: attach net monthly change to the full customer‑month matrix (0 if no activity)
WITH all_months AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
), all_customers AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT "customer_id"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
), calendar AS (
     SELECT c."customer_id",
            m."month_year"
     FROM   all_customers AS c
     CROSS  JOIN all_months AS m
)
SELECT cal."customer_id",
       cal."month_year",
       COALESCE(mv."monthly_change", 0) AS "monthly_change"
FROM   calendar AS cal
LEFT   JOIN (
        SELECT "customer_id",
               strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year",
               SUM(CASE 
                       WHEN "txn_type" = 'deposit'    THEN  "txn_amount"
                       WHEN "txn_type" = 'withdrawal' THEN - "txn_amount"
                       ELSE 0
                   END) AS "monthly_change"
        FROM   "customer_transactions"
        GROUP  BY "customer_id", "month_year"
) AS mv
ON     cal."customer_id" = mv."customer_id"
AND    cal."month_year"  = mv."month_year"
ORDER  BY cal."customer_id", cal."month_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 🔟 Description: FINAL – monthly change + cumulative closing balance for every customer, 
-- producing rows even for months without any activity.
WITH all_months AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
), all_customers AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT "customer_id"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
), calendar AS (
     SELECT c."customer_id",
            m."month_year"
     FROM   all_customers AS c
     CROSS  JOIN all_months AS m
), monthly_values AS (
     SELECT "customer_id",
            strftime('%Y-%m', "txn_date") AS "month_year",
            SUM(CASE 
                    WHEN "txn_type" = 'deposit'    THEN  "txn_amount"
                    WHEN "txn_type" = 'withdrawal' THEN - "txn_amount"
                    ELSE 0
                END) AS "monthly_change"
     FROM   "customer_transactions"
     GROUP  BY "customer_id", "month_year"
)
SELECT cal."customer_id",
       cal."month_year",
       COALESCE(mv."monthly_change", 0)                                     AS "monthly_change",
       SUM( COALESCE(mv."monthly_change", 0) )
           OVER (PARTITION BY cal."customer_id"
                 ORDER BY cal."month_year")                                  AS "closing_balance"
FROM   calendar AS cal
LEFT   JOIN monthly_values AS mv
       ON  cal."customer_id" = mv."customer_id"
       AND cal."month_year"  = mv."month_year"
ORDER  BY cal."customer_id", cal."month_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries build up step‑by‑step understanding and culminate in a complete, gap‑free month‑end balance report for every customer.
